# JOURNEY · draw on a Cathode Array: a dot with write and a whole byte with write_byte, on one rise.
# Crt's coil makes it a rail on d0, bit 0 of the bus d, so d reads 1. Its screen is narrowed to 8 dots
# (four braille cells, all inside the botfish's own body). The rail is addr, bit, byte and both strobes:
# write stores the bit at dot 1 (top row, second dot) and write_byte stores the byte 1 at byte 1, the
# second row's first dot. Both land in one cell, ⠊; without write_byte it reads ⠈, without write ⠂.
# Spent: Computer $8000 + botfish $7700 + Cathode Array $7700 + Inverter Coil $496 = $23896 of the
# 40,000 stake (scenes/start-with-a-stake.play).
# The panel walks by count: listens, drives, width, glyphs, addr, bit, write, byte, write_byte.

clear
include scenes/start-with-a-stake.play
include scenes/grow-a-matrixtank.play
include scenes/buy-at-the-bench.play "Inverter Coil" Fabric
include scenes/buy-at-the-bench.play "Cathode Array" Peripherals
include scenes/take-a-fish.play botfish crt

run /consume inverter coil
key enter
run /consume cathode array
expect Cathode Array to the botfishes
snap the install picker offers the Cathode Array to Crt
key enter
absent to the botfishes
run /freeze "Crt"

run /program "Crt"
key down
type d0
key down
key backspace 2
type 8
snap the screen is narrowed to eight dots
key down 2
expect glyphs
type d
key down
type d0
key down
type d0
key down
type d
key down
type d0
snap the rail is the address, the bit, the byte and both strobes
key enter
absent listens

tick 4
expect ⠊⠀⠀⠀
snap a dot and a byte on Crt's body
run /circuit
expect write ◂ d0
snap the circuit lists the screen's five wires under Crt
key esc
absent Circuit#
tick 40
expect ⠊⠀⠀⠀
snap the picture holds with the rail still high and nothing rising
